_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 1
---
order: 1
---
short_label: II.1
---
sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: If there are two straight lines, and one of them is cut into any number of segments whatever, then the rectangle contained by the two straight lines equals the sum of the rectangles contained by the uncut straight line and each of the segments.
----
proof:

Let {A} and {BC} be two straight lines, and let {BC} be cut at random at the points {D} and {E}.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="330" height="250" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img src="propII1.gif" alt="II.1"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
